-- ============================================================================
-- Migration 64: backfill NONE strict-typed `source` fields (Track R.0e).
--
-- Same drift class migration 61 fixed for `entity`, now on `source`. Track J's
-- migration 52 added `private ON source TYPE bool DEFAULT false`, but a
-- SurrealDB column DEFAULT applies only to NEWLY created records — rows that
-- predate the migration keep NONE. The strict `TYPE bool` then rejects them on
-- the first UPDATE. Because a SCHEMAFULL UPDATE re-validates the WHOLE record,
-- that one NONE blocks ANY write to the row, including the source-level
-- aggregate embedding write (R.0) and the app's own source updates:
--   "Found NONE for field `private`, with record `source:...`, but expected a bool"
--
-- SCOPE — verified empirically against the full 1->63 schema (INFO FOR TABLE
-- source + a per-field NONE-rejection probe on a fresh container): `private` is
-- the ONLY strict, non-`option<>`, no-VALUE field on `source`. Every other
-- field is either `option<...>` (asset, command, embedding, full_text,
-- metadata, title, topics, zotero_*), which accepts NONE legitimately, or has a
-- computed `VALUE` clause (created, updated), which can never be NONE. So
-- `private` is the only field that can block a write — but we also normalize
-- `topics` here because the legacy staging rows carry `topics = NONE` and `[]`
-- is the honest "no topics" value the read path expects. `topics` is
-- `option<array<string>>`, so this is data hygiene (NONE -> []), not a
-- writability fix; `private` is the load-bearing one.
--
-- Explicitly NOT touched: `embedding` is `option<array<float>>` where NONE is
-- intended ("aggregate not yet computed", migration 63) — coalescing it to []
-- would corrupt that signal.
--
-- This UPDATE coalesces each field to value-or-default. It is idempotent: on a
-- clean row every `field ?? default` is a no-op; on a drifted row it sets only
-- the NONE fields. No schema change.
-- ============================================================================

UPDATE source SET
    private = private ?? false,
    topics  = topics  ?? [];
